  "body": "Hello,\r\n\r\nI put my situation in context:\r\n\r\nI have a small example with webserial for arduino, when I raise my website from a server and access it from the machine that serves it, it works perfectly (localhost: <port>). But if I access this server (ip_server: port) from another machine, I get the error => TypeError: Cannot read property.\r\n\r\nI have in the code also added, so that it detects if serial is allowed in the browser and if it is not, it shows a message, and it also happens that when accessing from another machine, it is as if it did not recognize webserial:\r\n\r\nif ('serial' in navigator) {\r\n     const notSupported = document.getElementById ('notSupported');\r\n     notSupported.classList.add ('hidden');\r\n\r\n   }\r\n\r\nThank you for your collaboration, I am sorry if I have not explained correctly.",
